{"id": "EUVD-2026-79502", "enisaUuid": "07ecac68-b238-39f5-bf63-2a1c6c4eb13b", "description": "Netmaker makes networks with WireGuard. Prior to version 1.5.0, the `sqliteDeleteRecord` function in Netmaker's database layer constructs SQL `DELETE` statements using direct string concatenation of user-supplied input. This allows an authenticated attacker to perform boolean-based SQL injection. Version 1.5.0 fixes the issue.", "datePublished": "2026-09-15T19:49:26", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-16T17:46:00", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/gravitl/netmaker/security/advisories/GHSA-r8cr-4f9w-7r75", "https://github.com/gravitl/netmaker/releases/tag/v1.5.0"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-32599", "GHSA-r8cr-4f9w-7r75"], "assigner": "GitHub_M", "epss": 0.36, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1a3bda9a-974b-3490-a7c5-f670153de62f", "product": {"name": "netmaker", "vendor": {"name": "gravitl"}}, "product_version": "< 1.5.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "c7f08fd9-1564-3e38-8867-c9182cfbb4cd", "vendor": {"name": "gravitl"}}], "isExploited": false}